<form id="qr-passphrase-form" class="phonetic-form" autocomplete="off" novalidate>
  <div class="phonetic-field">
    <label for="qr-passphrase">QR passphrase</label>
    <input id="qr-passphrase" type="password" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="new-password" autocapitalize="off">
    <label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" id="show-qr-passphrase"> Show QR passphrase</label>
  </div>
  <p>Each transfer between the devices can use Super Base 58 lines or QR codes. QR codes are encrypted with this passphrase, so a camera or a person that sees the screen cannot read them. Enter the same passphrase on both devices. Use a new one for this, not the passphrase of your seed phrase. It is only needed for QR codes, and it is not saved.</p>
</form>
